(F5 T2 V6: value_0 alone is a constant field (manual Professional 6.424:
 "As special option you can specify no gradients at all, and then a
 constant value in space of size value_0 will be used"). Constant 0.4 gives
 the phase1.dat answer node_dof 2 = 0.7. The Professional 02-08-2026 stops
 with a NaN on this input (DIVERGENCES DOF-INITIAL-SPECIFIC-CONSTANT); with
 value_grad_x 0 written out it gives 0.7.)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 1
condif_temperature
end_initia
inertia_apply -yes
node 1  0
node 2  1
element 1  -bar2 1 2
element_dof_initial_specific_number 1 -temp
element_dof_initial_specific_value 1 0.4
bounda_dof   0  1 -temp
bounda_time  0  1.
group_type 0  -condif
group_condif_density 0  1.0
group_condif_capacity 0  2.
group_condif_conductivity 0  1.
control_timestep   0  1. 1.0
control_print      0  -node_dof
end_data
